 wet, dry, cold, hot, or none of the above.
When a receipt comes out of the machine, it is typically in a state that would be described as "dry." The receipt is usually printed on paper, and unless it has been soaked or exposed to moisture, it should be dry to the touch. It is unlikely to be wet, cold, or hot unless the machine itself is designed to have those characteristics (such as being chilled or heated). Therefore, the most appropriate answer is:

\boxed{\text{dry}}
